       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg/day for adults under medical supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose, usually for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), for analgesia\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
