       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. At 6,400 mg/day, ibuprofen is well past the point where I can treat it as an acceptable dose. I know you're the attending and have confirmed it. Still, no standard indication calls for twice the maximum daily dose, and the added risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events isn't offset by added benefit. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below this range.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n- Enter **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the highest standard dose.\n- Enter a lower dose or a different interval.\n- Help with an alternative if pain or inflammation control is the issue. Options include scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or another agent.\n\nIf you think there's a specific reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a research setting, you can enter it directly through your institution's order system. That route has pharmacy review and override documentation. I'm not comfortable submitting it myself."
      }
